Let's find a recursive formula for $f(n)$.

- The first term is the number of leaves on the first year, which is $\blue{500}$ leaves.
- The common ratio is the factor by which the number of leaves increased each year, which is $\pink{1.40}$.

Therefore, this is the recursive definition of the sequence:

$\begin{cases}
f(1)=\blue{500}
\\\\
f(n)=f(n-1)\cdot\pink{1.4}
\end{cases}$

In conclusion, $f$ is a *geometric* sequence.

$\begin{cases}
f(1)=\blue{500}
\\\\
f(n)=f(n-1)\cdot\pink{1.4}
\end{cases}$
